{{!-- SITES — interesting places the PCs can explore. The third of the Prep tab's three views
      (gm-toolkit-tab-prep.hbs), having been a section folded in at the foot of the Expeditions
      pane, before that a rail tab of its own here, and before that a tab on the steading sheet.

      WHY IT IS A VIEW BESIDE EXPEDITIONS AND NOT A SECTION UNDER IT. Its own first sentence says
      a site is "the destination of an expedition, a point of interest on the way, or an
      incidental discovery", which is why it was put under the trips in the first place. But a
      site is a page-long card and a world has a dozen of them, so under a full card list it was
      the one pane a GM had to scroll past every trip to reach. One click on the switcher is the
      same distance from the journey and no scroll from anything.

      NO HEADING AND NO FOLD, therefore. The switcher segment IS its heading, and a fold over the
      whole of a view would only be a second way to hide what the switcher already hides. Its old
      collapse key (`gm-expeditions-sites`) is retired with it: a GM who had folded it finds the
      view open, which is the right way round for a pane they have to ask for by name.

      A PANE OF THE PREP TAB'S OWN GROUP, `data-group="prep"`, which is what the switcher shows
      and hides. The sites masonry (gm-prep-masonry.js) needs nothing from that: a grid in a
      hidden pane measures zero and is left unpacked, and the pane being shown is the resize its
      observer is waiting for.

      THE STORAGE DID NOT MOVE and must not. A site is a JournalEntryPage inside a hidden
      per-steading JournalEntry, pointed at by a flag on the STEADING actor — see the header of
      module/actors/gmtoolkit/gm-prep-tabs.js, which spells out the silent data-loss path.

      NO PENCIL, unlike the Threats tab, and so no `stonetop-readonly` either. A pencil gates the
      fields you type into, and this pane has none: a site is written up in the wizard and
      re-opened in it, its d20 tables roll without writing anything, and the only control left is
      the trash. Gating that ONE button behind a pencil bought nothing and cost the obvious reading
      of the toolbar — the trash sat beside a live pencil and was simply mouse-dead, when the
      confirm dialog it already opens is the real "are you sure".

      The `steading-*` class names are CSS hooks kept deliberately; they and the storage rule are
      explained at length in gm-toolkit-tab-threats.hbs and in gm-prep-tabs.js. Every listener
      this pane needs is scoped to `.steading-sites` rather than to a panel, which is why each move
      it has made cost the mixin nothing. --}}
<div class="tab sites{{#if stonetop.prep.panes.sites.active}} active{{/if}}" data-group="prep" data-tab="sites"
     id="{{stonetop.prep.panes.sites.id}}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="{{stonetop.prep.panes.sites.tabId}}">
	<section class="sheet-tab steading-sites steading-prep-cards">

		{{#if stonetop.hasSteading}}
		{{!-- THE PANE BAR the other two views open on (gm-prep-pane-bar.hbs), inside
		      `.steading-sites` because that is the scope the "New site" handler is bound to. The
		      intro that used to stand here in full is behind the bar's "?" now. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-pane-bar" kind="site"
		    lead=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.lead")
		    intro=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.intro")
		    pane=stonetop.prep.panes.sites
		    label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.add")
		    bare=(not stonetop.sites.length)}}

		{{#if stonetop.sites.length}}
		<div class="steading-threats-grid">
			{{#each stonetop.sites}}
			<div class="threat-card-wrap" data-page-uuid="{{this.uuid}}">
				{{> "stonetop.site-card" this}}
				{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-card-tools" kind="site" uuid=uuid}}
			</div>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{else}}
		{{!-- No `accepts`: a site is written up in the wizard, not dragged in, so there is no row
		      of kinds to promise. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-empty" view="sites" kind="site"
		    title=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.emptyTitle")
		    text=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.empty")
		    label=(localize "stonetop.gmToolkit.sites.add")}}
		{{/if}}
		{{else}}
		{{> "stonetop.gm-prep-no-steading" noun="Sites"}}
		{{/if}}

	</section>
</div>
